WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.290
- I still, I look at it
now and I can't believe

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.320
that I'm in that scene.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.903
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.120
Can you believe this weather, Frank?

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.560
I'm Tony Provenzano and you
have Jimmy Hoffa, obviously,

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.863
and Frank and my cousin, and
we've come for the meeting.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.850
Because Hoffa needs my
endorsement to run again,

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.010
so he can get re-elected
for the teamsters.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.380
People freezing to death
in New York and look at us.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.700
- Luigi, hey.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.100
- Why we don't live here all year round

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.283
is what I wanna know.

00:00:34.283 --> 00:00:35.116
- Oh.

00:00:35.116 --> 00:00:36.050
- Beautiful.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.380
- It's summer.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.900
- What?

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.733
- It's summer.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.270
People aren't freezing
to death in New York.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.393
It's summer.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.750
- In my mind it's always eight degrees

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.330
in New York, I'm making a point.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.610
We're two egos that clash,
do you know what I mean?

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.040
We just shouldn't be in the
same room together, basically.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.530
And in this particular meeting,

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.680
it goes against everything
that Jimmy stands for

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.670
because he doesn't, you know
he's like I've just said,

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.490
he's a very stubborn man and to make

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:07.750
an apology for him would,
he just doesn't do that.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.910
So he needs my endorsement
to be able to run again

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.600
in the elections, so this
meeting's been called

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:16.830
for him to be able to ask me.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:17.803
- Making a point.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.069
Making a point dressing like that?

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:22.719
This how you dress for a meeting?

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.400
- This is how you dress in Florida?

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.490
In a suit?

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:28.627
- For a meeting?

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.080
Anywhere, Florida,
Timbuktu, I dress in a suit.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:33.960
For a meeting.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.520
- I mean the shirt's so
loud, it's so brilliant.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.120
We found an original shirt.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.290
He's got a pair of Gucci
loafers on, cream Gucci loafers.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.780
And we sprayed a bit of
fake tan on me and all that

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.470
and he, you know he's
loving while he's out there,

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.540
cause he's from New York, so
he's loving it in Florida.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.220
The shirt, it was an original pattern.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.970
I've still got one actually
in my wardrobe at home.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.599
Never to be worn again,
but it's for nostalgia,

00:01:57.599 --> 00:01:58.432
do you know what I mean?

00:01:58.432 --> 00:02:00.950
- I never waited for anyone who was late

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:04.750
more than ten minutes in my life.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.750
- I'd say fifteen, fifteen's right.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.970
- No, ten.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.270
- On the page, it's very
much, it's a much more,

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.640
it's very condensed that particular scene,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.710
and it's just dialogue between me and him.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.180
And Monty just, he kinda took me aside

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.200
and he just went,

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.310
"Just play with it a little
bit more, just free it up."

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.910
We did a couple of takes and that,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.567
and Stephen popped into my head,

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.910
my own voice popped into
my head and I was like,

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.160
I'm in a scene with Robert De Niro.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.850
And he doesn't say nothing on the page,

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:37.050
so my head went, Oh, I can't
have that, that it's just.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.600
And then it was about,
you know, being late

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.530
and I just turned to him and I just went,

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.234
What do you think, Frank?

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:45.420
And to just watch him go,
hm, and then he comes up with

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.810
that brilliant line of twelve and a half.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.210
Ten's not enough, you have
to take traffic into account.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:53.133
- That's what I'm doing, I'm
taking traffic into account.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.090
That's why it's ten.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.220
- I still say fifteen.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.133
- No, ten.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.350
- Fine, we disagree on that.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.210
- How bout twelve and a half minute?

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.360
- [Tony] There we go, twelve and half.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.512
- The middle, right in the middle.

00:03:04.512 --> 00:03:05.345
- [Tony] It's a compromise.
- Beautiful.

00:03:05.345 --> 00:03:08.940
- And to just watch him
pop into the scene then

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.304
and then we carried on and that bit

00:03:11.304 --> 00:03:13.140
where I stand up and go to walk away that,

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.600
you know that it wasn't scripted.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.840
- I asked for your endorsement

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.690
and you're giving me all this crap.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.047
- I asked for your apology.

00:03:18.047 --> 00:03:20.215
- Who the fuck are you to apologize to?

00:03:20.215 --> 00:03:21.550
- Jimmy, Jimmy.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.210
- Who the fuck are you?

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:24.292
- Kids be gentle.
- I don't need this, Jimmy.

00:03:24.292 --> 00:03:26.033
- Let's just sit down, Tony.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:28.000
- I need this, I need you?

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.440
- Yeah, you need me.
- Tony, please.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:30.634
- After we done one of the takes,

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:33.080
I went, is it all right
that I got up to make?

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.120
Still to these, because
these are two legends,

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.250
you know what I mean, they're two masters.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.900
They're the reason, part of the reason

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.080
why I'm an actor today.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.810
I went, is it all right
when I got up to walk away?

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.367
I went back in to Stephen,
and they were like,

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:44.537
"No no, it was great, it was fine!

00:03:44.537 --> 00:03:46.030
"You know it comes alive!"

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:49.660
Marty creates this
playground where you're,

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.490
you know you don't have to stick

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.160
to everything that's on the script.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.990
You're allowed to play
with it and create it

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.550
and make it as real as possible.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.330
Me and Al just really
started to improvise,

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:03.510
so it become like a real
battle between these two egos.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.630
And then it goes into that scene as well,

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:08.720
but this time he comes at
me, do you know what I mean?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.053
So, and then we just
roll around on the floor.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.180
It's handbags at dawn

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.717
and it's meant to be slightly pathetic.

00:04:14.717 --> 00:04:16.280
- (laughs) Are you out
of your fucking mind?

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.360
- I'll apologize for being late

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.840
after I kidnap your
granddaughter, rip her guts out

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.593
and send them to you
in a fucking envelope!

00:04:22.593 --> 00:04:23.426
- Ah.
(slams into table)

00:04:23.426 --> 00:04:27.010
(yelling)
(chair crashes to floor)

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.143
- Get him off, get him, come on Tony!

00:04:28.143 --> 00:04:30.690
- And we've had and altercation before

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:31.670
when we met in prison.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:32.890
I was owed two million quid,

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.800
which is a lot of money,
do you know what I mean?

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.220
Especially back then.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.053
- You lost it.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.510
You forfeited it, when you came in here.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.867
That's it, you know.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.380
- So yours forfeited too?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.336
In the altercation we had,

00:04:46.336 --> 00:04:48.050
he said something derogatory,

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.460
do you know what I mean, about Italians.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.380
So I've got the (foreign language)

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.010
- You people, you people.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:53.843
- What'd you say?

00:04:53.843 --> 00:04:54.676
- Oh my god.

00:04:54.676 --> 00:04:55.509
- What did you say?

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:56.413
- Ah come on what I said.

00:04:56.413 --> 00:04:58.299
What the fuck did I say,
I don't know what I said?

00:04:58.299 --> 00:04:59.480
- You people, you said you people.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.030
I'd already come up with an idea

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.700
at home when I was reading through.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.080
Whenever I had I little
idea to do something,

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.000
I didn't tell Marty and I didn't tell Al.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.520
I told the camera man and I asked

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.900
the props department how many

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.640
bowls of ice cream did they
have and they said, "loads."

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.000
And then I knew it was gonna be the last

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.920
take of the wide so I knew
I had to get this in before

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:17.880
otherwise you know what I mean

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.060
it wouldn't work if it
wasn't on the wide as well.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.259
So, he's eating the ice
cream really slowly really

00:05:23.259 --> 00:05:24.890
and his last little bit he took,

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:25.860
his last little mouthful

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.860
and he puts his spoon down in the bowl

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.160
and he just kinda leans back.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.937
What does that fucking mean, you people?

00:05:30.937 --> 00:05:35.100
- I'm done talking about this!

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:35.933
- You people?

00:05:35.933 --> 00:05:36.766
- I'm done.

00:05:36.766 --> 00:05:38.690
- As he did that, I just leaned across

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:43.367
and I just lashed his ice cream
bowl right across the room,

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:45.840
and I went to jump across
the table and I went you!

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.009
And he just went "Whoa!"

00:05:48.009 --> 00:05:48.842
You done?

00:05:48.842 --> 00:05:49.675
I'll rip your fucking head off!

00:05:49.675 --> 00:05:50.550
(ice cream bowl crashing on the floor)

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.840
Marty went, "and cut."

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.777
And he went, "(gasp)
did you see that Marty,

00:05:53.777 --> 00:05:54.957
"the kid frightened me?

00:05:54.957 --> 00:05:56.410
"He frightened me!"

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.380
So, we had this little you know

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.340
and then we got on like a house on fire,

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:01.173
do you know what I mean?

00:06:01.173 --> 00:06:02.690
I'd come across and then we'd stop

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:03.890
and then the stunt man would come in.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:04.868
- Fucking

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:07.117
(yelling)
(loud punching)

00:06:07.117 --> 00:06:08.066
(screams)

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:10.380
- I think I really caught
the fellow once in the ribs,

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:11.920
accidentally, completely.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.649
I know they're stunt men,
it's what they get paid for

00:06:13.649 --> 00:06:14.482
do you know what I mean.

00:06:14.482 --> 00:06:15.839
(yelling)

00:06:15.839 --> 00:06:16.672
- Hey, get off him.

00:06:16.672 --> 00:06:17.505
- I'll fucking kill you!

00:06:17.505 --> 00:06:18.517
I'll fucking kill you!

00:06:18.517 --> 00:06:21.650
But that moment where I did
smash his ice cream away,

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.240
he really got frightened,

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:24.800
you know what I mean as the character.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.420
So that was fantastic.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.080
And we just kind of carried that

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.870
into those little spats
that we had really.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:31.700
He'd just lean across
and he'd touch me hand

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.620
a couple of times, and he'd
just he'd just give me this

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.290
little nod and this little smile,

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.850
which made me feel really comfortable

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.000
and you know it's that little recognition

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.340
of well done, well done, well done.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.980
He called me the "kid" which was lovely,

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:44.826
do you know what I mean.

00:06:44.826 --> 00:06:47.826
(upbeat Jazz music)

